---
import FlowShot from '../FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import shotGallery from '../../../assets/flow/shots/flow-image-gallery-shot.webp';
import detailGalleryWords from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-gallery-words.webp';
import detailGalleryCollection from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-gallery-collection.webp';
---
<section class="border-t border-border/60 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-pictures">
  <div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Pictures</p>
      <h3 id="tour-pictures" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]">Change the picture. Keep the line.</h3>
      <p class="of-lede mt-5" data-animate="rise">Open a picture in Flow's gallery, choose another file from the same folder, and the document updates one Markdown line. Nothing else moves. The folder is the collection; Flow uploads, indexes, and duplicates nothing into a private library.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="of-stage of-stage--pad-top mt-12" data-animate="plate">
      <FlowShot src={shotGallery} alt="Orionfold Flow with a picture rendered in a document and the image gallery open on the same file." crop sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 78rem, (min-width: 1024px) 64rem, 100vw" />
      <FlowDetail class="of-stage__detail of-stage__detail--tr gallery-words-crop" src={detailGalleryWords} alt="Alt text and Title fields in Flow's image gallery." caption="You write the description · Flow does not guess" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 30rem, (min-width: 1024px) 27rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" animate />
    </div>
    <div class="mx-auto mt-12 grid max-w-5xl items-center gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
      <div>
        <p class="flow-path__num">Your folder, on screen</p>
        <h4 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">Add by file, drop, or paste.</h4>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">Flow copies a new picture into the folder and never moves the original or overwrites different bytes under the same name. Alt text and title are yours to type. Cropping, filters, and private Markdown syntax stay out.</p>
      </div>
      <FlowDetail src={detailGalleryCollection} alt="Flow's image gallery grouped by folder, with the document's pictures first and the current picture marked." caption="The document first · Then each folder" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 36rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" />
    </div>
    <details class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-5xl rounded-2xl border border-border/70 bg-surface px-5">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer py-4 font-semibold">What the gallery changes, and what it does not</summary>
      <ul class="flow-list pb-5">
        <li>The gallery proposes nothing and writes nothing on its own. You type the alt text and title.</li>
        <li>A swap changes that one line. Opening and browsing changes nothing on disk, byte for byte.</li>
        <li>Flow keeps no library of its own. It copies a new picture into your folder, so the original stays exactly where it was, and it never overwrites different bytes under the same name.</li>
        <li>No cropping, resizing, or filters. Markdown has no portable way to preserve them.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>
    <p class="of-spec-fine mx-auto mt-8 max-w-3xl text-center uppercase tracking-[0.14em]">Captured 2026-08-21 on the running build. The document, client, and figures are invented demo data.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    :global(.of-stage .gallery-words-crop.gallery-words-crop) { margin-top: 0; }
  }
</style>
